    <string name="robotics_legend_joints">Blue: revolute joints (R). Orange: prismatic (P). Green: the tool\'s trace (the shape of the workspace). In the DH frames: x orange, y green, z blue.</string>
    <string name="robotics_gimbal_lock">Gimbal lock: the first and third rotations act on the same axis and one degree of freedom is lost.</string>
    <string name="robotics_kutzbach_title">Grübler–Kutzbach in space</string>
    <string name="robotics_kutzbach_hint">Pick an example or count yourself: N links (base included) and how many pairs of each kind.</string>
    <string name="robotics_kutzbach_serial">Open chain: the DOF are the sum of its joints\' DOF.</string>
    <string name="robotics_kutzbach_stewart">Six extending legs move the platform in all 6 DOF of space: a parallel robot.</string>
    <string name="robotics_kutzbach_delta">It gives 9, but 6 are idle spins of each bar about its own axis between two ball joints (passive DOF): the Delta robot has 3 translational DOF.</string>
    <string name="robotics_kutzbach_rssr">It gives 2, but one is the coupler spinning about its axis between the ball joints: in practice, 1 DOF.</string>
    <string name="robotics_kutzbach_planar">It gives −2 and still moves: its parallel axes make several constraints redundant. Planar mechanisms are counted with the planar formula.</string>
